      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is unintuitive: create a `ConcurrentTest` with `NUM_THREADS` and then expect here `NUM_THREADS * 2` successful operations.\n\nI see that this is because the `ConcurrentTest.setup` has a for loop with `NUM_THREADS * 2` operations but I don\u0027t understand why and why every caller has to be aware of that. Either expect here exactly `NUM_THREADS` successful operations or encapsulate the verification inside the `ConcurrentTest` class.",
