      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T15:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the count if hardcoded to `1` what is the purpose of this `CountDownLatch` when we run multiple threads? AFAIU, the idea is to synchronize all the tasks on that latch and then let them all proceed at about the same time. However, the latch counter will be down to zero after the first thread calls await and when other threads call await it will exit immediatelly.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 189,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 189,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "624a600b096530ce89fd1653488b94cfc841b7b9",
